    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0436" n="1250" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg1250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Dulles papers, “Telephone
                    Conversations”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d123-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1953-12-01">December 1,
                            1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Secretary telephoned Mr. Bowie and said he thought the Candor Speech was
                    likely to see the light of day, at least to the point of bringing it up as a
                    proposal at Bermuda.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d123-f2"/> The President went over it
                    last night and marked it up. He did quite a bit in the direction of cutting out
                    some of the stuff that could be offensive to the Soviet Union, although he
                    didn’t believe he did a great deal of toning down in other respects. Bowie
                    wanted to know how we would get our oar in and the Secretary said he would call
                    the White House and ask for a copy of the draft as soon as it is retyped.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion of other subjects.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d123-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d123-f1-content">
